

Run the project in Ubuntu and generate the real output with:

```bash
cd ~/capstone-temp-monitor
sudo ./app/temp_monitor --reset
sudo ./app/temp_monitor --drift 40 | tee output/temperature_output.txt
```

Let the program run until you capture NORMAL, WARNING, and CRITICAL states,
then press `Ctrl+C`.

The resulting `temperature_output.txt` is intentionally generated from the
actual Ubuntu VM run rather than using fabricated readings.
